 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S443-011\", \"clauses\": {\"identify\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"The {perim_label} is the total distance around the {shape}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 states what the perimeter of a named plane figure is (perim_label is always the word perimeter from F01; shape is rectangle, square or triangle). No printed family asks the learner to pick out or name a figure from several, so this is the closest match.\"}, \"measure\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"A {shape} has sides {l} cm and {w} cm. What is its perimeter?\", \"reasoning\": \"F10 gives two side lengths in centimeters (l and w, from 1 to 13 excluding 10 and 12) that the learner measures and combines. No printed text tells the learner to use a measuring tool, so measure is addressed only through the lengths in cm.\"}, \"perimeter\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"A square has a side of {s} cm. What is its perimeter?\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 asks for the perimeter of a square from one side length in cm (s from the sides domain, members 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 9, 10, 13), which requires the four equal sides to be combined.\"}, \"plane_figure\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"A {shape} has sides {l} cm and {w} cm. What is its perimeter?\", \"reasoning\": \"The shape slot prints the plane figure rectangle, and the question is about that figure's perimeter. The shape domain for F10 is a repeat of the generated value and was printed only as rectangle.\"}, \"tools\": {\"verdict\": \"NOT_PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": null, \"template\": null, \"reasoning\": \"No printed family names a ruler, a measuring tool or any tool. The declared task_type variants (identify_and_measure, measure_tools) do not change any printed text: template_chosen_by_values lists only shape or nothing, so no family's wording differs by task_type.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F04\", \"F05\", \"F09\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"A square has 4 equal sides, each {s} {count_noun} long.\", \"Add all three sides: {a} + {b} + {c} = {answer}.\", \"Perimeter = 2 × ({l} + {w}) = 2 × {v} = {answer}.\", \"A triangle has sides {a} cm, {b} cm, and {c} cm. What is its perimeter?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03: the count_noun slot (unit or units, derived from sides) is not tied to the s slot, so the template can print a length of 1 with the plural noun, or a length above 1 with the singular noun. Both are ungrammatical for a grade 2 reader. F04: the template has no shape choice (template_chosen_by_values is empty), so the hint 'Add all three sides' can appear on rectangle and square problems, which have four sides. That is a false statement. F05: the template groups a sum with parentheses before multiplying by 2. 'order of operations' is listed in NOT_YET_KNOWN, and the grouping is the concept it gates. The sides domain (1 to 13, distinct in every render) feeds l and w. F09: a, b and c are each drawn independently from 1 to 13 (distinct_in_every_render is false, and no constraint links them). So the triangle can be given sides that cannot close into a triangle (for example 1 cm, 1 cm and 13 cm). The statement 'A triangle has sides ...' is then false about the figure. No fault found in F01, F02, F06, F07, F08 or F10. The words 'distance', 'width' and 'add' are not in NOT_YET_KNOWN and are not treated as gate breaches. F10 names only rectangle, so the ambiguity of 'has sides' for a rectangle is not flagged.\"}",
